  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want a smiley or inline image to sit **on the text baseline**, with its bottom level with the bottom of the text, rather than centred vertically on the line. A message full of smileys then reads like HFR and legacy. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17, device screenshot: two large animated smileys centred on their text line, overhanging above and below.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Resources/reader.css:133-134`:\n\n```css\n/* Smileys (every image that is not a posted picture) sit on the text line. */\n.content img:not(.hfrplusimg), .signature img:not(.hfrplusimg) { vertical-align: middle; }\n```\n\nThis dates from LOT-083 (#257).\n\n### Legacy @ 87fe0d1c\n\nThe reader sheets `SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/style-liste-*.css` set no `vertical-align` on message images (`git grep vertical-align 87fe0d1c -- 'SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/style-liste-*.css'` finds nothing). Message images therefore use the CSS default, `baseline`: the bottom of the image sits on the text baseline. The `vertical-align: middle` rules of `style-smile.css` (:27, 131, 137, 173) style the smiley picker, not message content. Check this when you port it.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Message and signature smileys and inline images align on the text baseline (`vertical-align: baseline`, or the default) in every theme.\n- Posted pictures (`.hfrplusimg`) are unchanged.\n- Check that a small smiley on a line of normal text keeps the same line height as legacy, so no line grows taller than it does there.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A CSS test that the rule no longer sets `middle`.\n- An app-hosted WebKit test: in a line with a smiley taller than the text, the image's bottom equals the text baseline (±1 px).\n- Tests fail without the change.\n- A `### Ledger` `changelog` entry: a parity fix citing the legacy sheets.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nThe message in the screenshot: both smileys rest on their text line.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
